  "approach": "Teach the one rule of basic negation (no goes right before the verb), with the survival negatives the learner will say most, the \"No, no ...\" answer, and a check on the English do-support habit.",
  "coverage": [
    "No goes right before the verb: No entiendo, No quiero, No tengo",
    "Spanish has no helper verb like \"do\": No entiendo, never No hago entiendo",
    "Answering: No, no tengo. The first no answers, the second negates the verb",
    "Survival negatives: No sé (I don't know), No entiendo (I don't understand), No hablo inglés",
    "With chunks: No voy a trabajar. No hay agua. No necesito ayuda.",
    "No is never placed after the verb: Entiendo no is wrong"
  ],
